# ── GHSA-72r4-9c5j-mj57 — pnpm 11.4.0, fixed in 10.34.4 / 11.7.0 ──────────────
#
# "pnpm: `patch-remove` could delete project-selected files"
#
# WHY SUPPRESSED RATHER THAN PATCHED. pnpm is a BUILD tool baked into the upstream
# Firecrawl image. Our Dockerfile applies Debian security patches with apt-get, which
# cannot touch an npm-managed package — so this is not fixable from our layer. It needs
# upstream to bump pnpm and republish.
#
# WHY THE RISK IS ACCEPTED. The advisory is about `pnpm patch-remove` deleting files in
# the project directory it is run against. Nothing in the running container invokes pnpm:
# the images run `node dist/...` entrypoints against an already-installed tree. It is a
# developer-workstation concern reaching us only because the tool ships in the image.
#
# NOT A BLANKET SUPPRESSION. This is one advisory id. The gate stays at CRITICAL,HIGH with
# ignore-unfixed, so any other fixable HIGH still fails the build.
#
# REVIEW: remove this entry once the upstream image ships pnpm >= 11.7.0. `make
# image-digests` reports when the base has moved, which is the trigger to re-check.
# Suppressed 2026-09-02, on the operator ruling to accept and proceed.
GHSA-72r4-9c5j-mj57
